  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Sustainable livelihoods in the context of climate change</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Fundaci&#xf3;n Nuna works in the Department of La Paz on sustainable rural development and community organisation.  The organisation supports communities to achieve improvements in sustainable agricultural production in order to reduce their vulnerability to the impact of climate change through technical training. They also seek to strengthen local municipal management and civic participation to promote transparency and accountability, in particular the participation and skills of women. Fundaci&#xf3;n Nuna places strong emphasis on working with young people and on gender. This project in the municipality of Ancoraimes near Lake Titicaca, Curva and Mocomocowill work towards increasing awareness of the causes and impact of climate change at municipal and community level. Small-scale farming households will receive training and technical accompaniment in sustainable and innovative agricultural practices aiming to increase their production and also reduce their vulnerability to the impact of climate change.</narrative>
  </description>
